Yes, it does actually - very well.  In fact, I was already leaning toward the "wrapper + descriptor" approach (with some discovery) as follows:
1) wrapper + descriptor : this would be the fundamental algorithm used by the application.  I want the user to be in full control of which applications are integrated into the desktop environment.  The descriptor is key to a human readable config file and offers future feature expansion opportunities.  
2) discovery : for convenience, the desktop environment could scan the pre-defined "plugins" directory for plugins it does not already recognize (which requires yet another config file that we have not discussed yet).  While not strictly necessary, this feature enhances user experience and helps control the "onboarding" of new applications by providing a user interface to help guide the user in proper setup.

